# Prepares the built fixture underdark-deepgnome-seed3-opt0818 for the checks that load it (bd inc-10v7f).
# The old fixture, a .sav, held this state: wizard mode on with Free Advancement; the deep gnome Rogue raised
# to level 6 (Toughness at level 3, Blind Fight at level 6), and the new skill ranks spent. The deep gnome's
# racial innate spells (Cause Blindness, Passwall, ...) arrive with levels, so a check that reads them needs it.
# Ruling V7-1: a fixture holds only the created character, so the checks that need the state make it here.
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                       # character sheet

# Level to 3, where the third feat is offered, and to 6 for the fourth.
# Pressing G until the menu appears is safer than counting levels: it does
# not care which levels a rogue is given a feat at.
@until "Choose a feat" G
# Toughness is drawn as "[ ] Toughness": the feat list is longer than the 52
# letters LMenu has to give out, so the entries past the 52nd get a blank
# bracket. A menu ignores the space bar, so the only way in is to put the
# cursor on the row and press ENTER.
@cursorto "Toughness" DOWN
ENTER
@until "Choose a feat" G
@choose "Blind Fight"
@expect "Rogue 6"

S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*9
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*9
@cursorto:mark "Climb" UP
RIGHT*9
ENTER y
@until "Things in View" ESC
